ecific deep residual network architecture used as a backbone.', 'A smaller backbone network used in the study.', 'A specific backbone network architecture used in the pose estimation head.', 'A backbone model used in FastPose.', 'A backbone model used in FastPose. FastPose-18 is used as a backbone model.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 8, 9]}, 'Scale-Normalized Image and Feature Pyramids (SIFP)': {'description': ['A paradigm that exploits scale-normalized image and feature pyramids to address the scale variation problem, boosting both performance and speed.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 11]}, 'pose estimation': {'description': ['The task of identifying and locating keypoints of a person in an image or video.', 'The task of determining the positions of key body joints or landmarks in an image or video frame.', 'The task of determining the configuration of a human body, typically by identifying key points such as joints.', 'One of the tasks integrated by MTN in the FastPose framework.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2, 11, 7]}, 'multi-person pose estimation': {'description': ['The task of estimating poses of multiple people in an image or video.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2, 4]}, 'pose tracking': {'description': ['The task of tracking the poses of people over time in a video.', 'The task of tracking human poses across video frames.', 'The objective of tracking human poses in videos.', 'Performed by an occlusion-aware strategy.', 'The task of tracking the pose of a person or object over time.', 'The objective of tracking human poses over time.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2, 3, 8, 9, 11]}, 'Flow-based pose similarity': {'description': ['A metric used to measure the similarity of poses based on optical flow.', 'A metric used for solving the matching problem.', 'A metric exploited in [50] to solve the matching problem in a greedy fashion.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Scale-normalized image and feature pyramid (SIFP)': {'description': ['A paradigm proposed to address scale variation issues in pose estimation.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [11, 3]}, 'Articulated multi-person pose tracking': {'description': ['The task of tracking poses of multiple people in videos, considering their articulated nature.', 'The specific application or domain where the pose tracking is being applied.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Articulated Multi-Person Pose Tracking in Videos': {'description': ['The specific application or domain where the pose tracking is being applied.', "The task of tracking multiple people's poses in video."], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 4]}, 'Scale-normalized image pyramid and feature pyramid (SIFP)': {'description': ['A paradigm exploited to alleviate the scale variation problem of MTN.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [11, 5]}, 'Feature Pyramid': {'description': ['A hierarchical representation of image features, often used to address scale variation by processing features at different levels of detail.', 'A multi-scale representation of features used in SIFP.'], 'type': ['generic', 'method'], 'source_chunk_index': [5, 7]}, 'Head networks': {'description': ['Networks applied separately to each RoI for human detection, pose estimation, and person Re-ID.', 'The network architecture built upon the backbone and RPN within the MTN framework.'], 'type': ['generic', 'method'], 'source_chunk_index': [6, 7]}, 'MTN network': {'description': ['The specific network being discussed, whose application and architecture are being described.', 'A unified network performing human detection, pose estimation, and person Re-ID simultaneously.', '